 reason for his visit is  different this time as the power itself  has been compromised and is in a  weakened state  and so the unit power seeks to bond with  the hulk and replicate his power  and also wants banner's assistance in  finding a scientist named dr gilbert  wiles earth's foremost expert  on the unipower to try and figure out  why it is weakening and so banner is  initially hesitant to help  because dr wiles is in manhattan and  he's afraid that if he turns into the  hulk he'll be a threat to all the people  there  and we learn the reason that he's in the  wilderness is to be far enough away from  civilization  that nobody will get hurt if he  transforms and so after receiving  assurance from the unipower that the  hulk ego  is being repressed banner goes to  manhattan and finds dr wiles now wanting  to conceal his true identity  banner introduces himself to dr wiles as  bruce barnes who's looking for  information about the unipower  shortly thereafter they're joined by dr  david garrett who says he's bankrolling  weil's research  in hopes that unlocking the secret of  the unipower will be beneficial for  mankind  suddenly garrett gets a call from agents  from advanced idea mechanics that are on  board a submarine that inform garrett  that the unit power  is currently inside banner meanwhile  wiles tells garrett that he was also  once the host of the unipower when a  plane he was on was hijacked and he was  able to use his powers to thwart the  hijackers and safely land the plane  then as swiftly as it arrived the power  left him and had been searching for more  knowledge of it ever since now garrett  then announces that he knows of the unit  power's presence within banner and fires  a beam at him that drives the unit power  from banner  hulk of course then takes over and is  immediately attacked by two robots that  were flanking garrett now once the aim  agents realize who they're dealing with  they opened up their entire arsenal to  fight the hulk  including weapons that had not yet been  tested and so hulk quickly gains the  upper hand but is soon  overpowered by the robots who hit him  with a beam of some energy that appears  to cause him great distress  however the unit power reappears and  merges with the hulk again  and once again turns him into the blue  version of the hulk now with the powers  of captain  universe hulk remarks now hulk is really  the strongest one there is suggesting  that his power level far surpasses  any power that he's ever encountered  hulk easily defeats the robots that were  attacking him and turns around to see  the body of david garrett with dr wiles  standing over him now hulk concludes  that wiles has killed garrett which he  thinks was the right thing to do  obviously but wiles informs him that it  was actually the bonding process between  the unipower and the hulk that produced  a flash of energy that killed garrick  and so as the police descend upon the  scene  hulk wants to stay and fight the banner  convinces him to leave which results in  wiles being arrested for garrett's  murder now later we see bruce banner  calling matt murdock from a pay phone  and that's where the issue ends and this  would actually go on to be a crossover  series where the unit power  is passed from hero to hero and so in  the next issue which reveals that matt  murdock has agreed to represent wiles  the unit power  bonds with daredevil and then of course  it goes on from there now maybe we'll  cover this story  if it's something that you guys are  interested in but for now we'll just  focus on the blue hole as i said earlier  this  is unfortunately all that we get to see  of the blue hulk the unit power leaves  him and as far as i know  never bonds with him again and the  really disappointing part of the hulk  having this power for such a short  period of time  is that we don't get to see him use the  power to his full potential not by a  long shot he just  beats up some robots and then leaves and  